{"title": "Where Pilot Fits with TCP, gRPC, and NATS", "slug": "pilot-vs-tcp-grpc-nats-comparison", "section": "blog", "description": "Compare TCP, gRPC, NATS, and Pilot by responsibility: transport, typed RPC, brokered messaging, agent identity, and cross-network reachability.", "seoTitle": "Where Pilot Fits with TCP, gRPC and NATS | Pilot Protocol", "author": "Pilot Protocol editorial team", "publishedAt": "2026-02-04T12:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["comparison", "grpc", "nats"], "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "TCP, gRPC, NATS, and Pilot solve different layers of an agent system. Treating them as interchangeable leads to the wrong comparison: TCP moves bytes, gRPC defines typed remote calls, NATS routes messages through a broker, and Pilot provides identity-aware reachability across networks.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This guide maps those responsibilities so you can combine the right tools instead of forcing one protocol to do every job. If your primary decision is between brokered messaging and typed RPC, start with our focused ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "NATS versus gRPC guide", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/learn/nats-vs-grpc-agent-messaging", "newTab": false}, "id": "6a49d33954137aa11bdf63eb"}, {"type": "text", "text": ".", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Four Tools, Four Different Jobs", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Raw TCP", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " provides a reliable, ordered byte stream between reachable endpoints. Your application supplies message framing, serialization, authentication, encryption, discovery, and retry behavior.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "gRPC", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "https://grpc.io", "newTab": true}, "id": "4ca21dde27669531fb887e78"}, {"type": "text", "text": " provides contract-first remote procedure calls over HTTP/2. Protocol Buffers, streaming, deadlines, and interceptors make it a strong application interface once clients can reach a server.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "NATS", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "https://nats.io", "newTab": true}, "id": "5429e6bbe83fc1c429aed23c"}, {"type": "text", "text": " provides brokered publish/subscribe and request/reply messaging. Core NATS emphasizes low-latency delivery; JetStream adds configurable persistence and replay.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Pilot Protocol", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " provides an overlay for agent identity, discovery, reachability, and encrypted peer paths. Its registry and beacon coordinate discovery and traversal; payloads take a direct encrypted path when possible and use an encrypted relay fallback when necessary.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Capability and Responsibility Matrix", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "table", "children": [{"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Concern", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "TCP", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph